{"Name":"Close Detection","Description":"Deprecated. Close a Crowdstrike Falcon detection. Note: Action \"Update Detection\" is the best practice for this use case.","Script":"from SiemplifyAction import SiemplifyAction\nfrom SiemplifyUtils import output_handler\nfrom ScriptResult import EXECUTION_STATE_COMPLETED, EXECUTION_STATE_FAILED\n\nfrom TIPCommon.extraction import extract_configuration_param, extract_action_param\n\nfrom constants import INTEGRATION_NAME, CLOSE_DETECTION_SCRIPT_NAME, API_ROOT_DEFAULT\nfrom CrowdStrikeManager import CrowdStrikeManager\n\n\n@output_handler\ndef main():\n    siemplify = SiemplifyAction()\n    siemplify.script_name = CLOSE_DETECTION_SCRIPT_NAME\n\n    siemplify.LOGGER.info(\"----------------- Main - Param Init -----------------\")\n\n    api_root = extract_configuration_param(\n        siemplify,\n        provider_name=INTEGRATION_NAME,\n        param_name=\"API Root\",\n        default_value=API_ROOT_DEFAULT,\n    )\n    client_id = extract_configuration_param(\n        siemplify, provider_name=INTEGRATION_NAME, param_name=\"Client API ID\"\n    )\n    client_secret = extract_configuration_param(\n        siemplify, provider_name=INTEGRATION_NAME, param_name=\"Client API Secret\"\n    )\n    use_ssl = extract_configuration_param(\n        siemplify,\n        provider_name=INTEGRATION_NAME,\n        param_name=\"Verify SSL\",\n        input_type=bool,\n        is_mandatory=True,\n    )\n    customer_id = extract_configuration_param(\n        siemplify,\n        provider_name=INTEGRATION_NAME,\n        param_name=\"Customer ID\",\n        print_value=True,\n    )\n\n    siemplify.LOGGER.info(\"----------------- Main - Started -----------------\")\n\n    detection_id = extract_action_param(\n        siemplify, param_name=\"Detection ID\", is_mandatory=True\n    )\n    hide_detection = extract_action_param(\n        siemplify, param_name=\"Hide Detection\", input_type=bool, print_value=True\n    )\n\n    result_value = True\n    status = EXECUTION_STATE_COMPLETED\n\n    try:\n        manager = CrowdStrikeManager(\n            client_id=client_id,\n            client_secret=client_secret,\n            use_ssl=use_ssl,\n            api_root=api_root,\n            customer_id=customer_id,\n        )\n\n        manager.close_detection(\n            detection_id, show_in_ui=False if hide_detection else True\n        )\n\n        output_message = f\"Successfully closed detection with id: {detection_id}.\"\n    except Exception as e:\n        output_message = (\n            f\"Error executing action '{CLOSE_DETECTION_SCRIPT_NAME}'. Reason: {e}\"\n        )\n        status = EXECUTION_STATE_FAILED\n        siemplify.LOGGER.error(output_message)\n        siemplify.LOGGER.exception(e)\n        result_value = False\n\n    siemplify.LOGGER.info(\"----------------- Main - Finished -----------------\")\n    siemplify.LOGGER.info(\n        f\"\\n  status: {status}\\n  is_success: {result_value}\\n  output_message: {output_message}\"\n    )\n    siemplify.end(output_message, result_value, status)\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n","IntegrationIdentifier":"CrowdStrikeFalcon","ScriptResultName":"is_success","DynamicResultsMetadata":null,"Creator":"Admin","IsEnabled":true,"IsCustom":true,"AiGenerated":false,"IsSystem":false,"Version":1.0,"TimeoutSeconds":600,"IsAsync":null,"AsyncPollingIntervalInSeconds":300,"TotalIntervalTimeoutForAsyncInSeconds":3600,"Parameters":[{"CustomActionId":0,"IsMandatory":true,"DefaultValue":"","Description":"Specify the id of the detection that needs to be closed.","Name":"Detection ID","Value":"","Type":0,"OptionalValues":null,"OptionalValuesJson":null},{"CustomActionId":0,"IsMandatory":false,"DefaultValue":"true","Description":"If enabled, action will hide the detection in the UI.","Name":"Hide Detection","Value":"true","Type":1,"OptionalValues":null,"OptionalValuesJson":null}],"DefaultResultValue":null,"PythonVersion":"None","ActionType":1,"SimulationData":{"Entities":[]},"SimulationDataJson":"{\"Entities\": []}","AICategories":[],"AIDescription":"### General Description\nThe **Close Detection** action allows users to programmatically close a specific detection within the CrowdStrike Falcon platform. This action is primarily used for remediation and workflow automation, enabling the resolution of security incidents directly from Google SecOps. It updates the status of a detection to 'closed' and provides an option to hide or show the detection in the CrowdStrike Falcon console UI.\n\n### Parameters Description\n| Parameter | Type | Mandatory | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Detection ID | String | Yes | The unique identifier (Composite ID or Detection ID) of the detection in CrowdStrike Falcon that should be closed. |\n| Show In UI | Boolean | No | If set to `True`, the detection will remain visible in the CrowdStrike Falcon console after being closed. If `False` (default), the detection will be hidden from the UI. |\n\n### Flow Description\n1. **Parameter Extraction**: The action retrieves the `Detection ID` and the `Show In UI` preference from the user input.\n2. **API Interaction**: It utilizes the `CrowdStrikeManager` to send a `PATCH` request to the CrowdStrike detections endpoint (`/detects/entities/detects/v2`).\n3. **Status Update**: The request payload specifies the target detection ID, sets the status to `closed`, and applies the visibility setting.\n4. **Response Validation**: The action verifies the API response to ensure the detection was successfully updated in the external system.\n\n### Additional Notes\nThis is a containment/remediation action that modifies the state of an external system. It does not perform data enrichment or modify internal Google SecOps entity attributes.","EntityTypes":[]}